WEBVTT

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.250
Morning!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.630
Oh, morning!

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.790
Feed Store Room 
 (Biological Production Association: Practicum Room)

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.460
<b>Cafeteria</b>

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.920
Thanks for the food!

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.510
Yum!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.600
All right, on to the next job!

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.720
<b>Campus Motto
Defy Logic  Cooperation  Diligence</b>

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.680
Language Arts 
Quiz

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.560
"Udders and Lactation"

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.270
Feed Store Room 
 (Biological Production Association: Practicum Room)

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.030
See you tomorrow.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.490
Yum!

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.250
It's already time for finals.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.700
I guess I'll review stuff for a bit...

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.700
Night.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.630
Lights out!

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.930
<b>Fall Chapter, Episode 1

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:48.710
Mikage!

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.980
Oh, are you done with club stuff?

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.830
Yup.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.650
Are you still finishing up 
your morning practicum?

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.170
A cow started giving birth right 
as we were about to finish.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.670
I'm covered in muck.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.710
Shouldn't you get changed quickly?

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.480
I'd like to...

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.160
But I'm looking for a bra.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.990
B...ra...

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:10.850
...ssiere.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.570
You can't find it?

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.420
Nope.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.880
I washed it because 
it was dirty, but...

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.870
M-Maybe someone stole it?

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.740
What? Ew, that'd suck!

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.590
Those aren't cheap, you know?

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.490
Th-Then that's really unforgivable!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.640
Right?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.850
Can you help me look for it?

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.430
Sure!

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.770
Thanks! You're so helpful!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.870
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What kind is it?

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.470
It's black and big.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.990
Black...

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.780
I wonder if the Holstein Club
 might know something.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.960
<b>Equestrian Club</b>

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.050
Oh, Hachiken-kun.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.960
What the hell is the Hol Club up to?

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.440
We're grooming the cow 
for the cattle show.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.950
Cattle show?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.430
It's a cow beauty pageant.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.620
Here, that's what it's like.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.420
Oh, the cow porn mag.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.390
Porn mag?

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.350
Hmm...

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.400
The Hol Club's cow's back 
is more rounded, isn't it?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.550
Oh, right.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:17.770
Hang on a sec.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.320
If you put her front legs on 
slightly higher ground, see?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.960
The line of her back looks straighter.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:28.700
You're right!

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.200
You can also let the hair grow 
longer where the back dips

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:37.130
and trim it short where the back's
raised to make it look even.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.890
Oh, I see.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.560
So that's how you fake it.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.880
More like, that's how we slave 
away to make her look beautiful!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.710
It's warpaint makeup, okay?!

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:47.590
I'm sorry!

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:48.890
You're beautiful!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.360
You're the best!

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.950
I'll never let any other man touch you!

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.270
Well, of course, the judges can see 
through stuff like that right away.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.600
Huh, okay.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.930
Oh, I forgot! I need to find that bra!

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.670
A bra?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.590
Oh, it's hanging out to 
dry in the club room.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:07.950
What size you need?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.800
Large, please.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.660
Oh, big ones, eh?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.490
What's this?

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.890
A bra for cows.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.850
When their udders get too large,

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.980
cows step on them and hurt themselves.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.530
Ah, so that's the bra...

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.450
Ow!

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.940
This semester is chock-full of events

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:41.680
Ezonoo Festival

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.540
like the Ezonoo Festival 
and the Freshman War.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.140
You may neglect your studies,

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.650
but remember that you can't compete in 
sports meets if you fail your finals.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.520
Good luck, Tokiwa.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.120
Sure.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.950
Komaba, are you gonna be pitching again?

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.080
Yeah, the next one's 
probably my third game.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.640
Wow, that's amazing!

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.270
I can't make it because of 
club duties, but good luck!

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.050
Oh, thanks.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.990
Oh, Hachiken.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.930
You sent some bacon to my family, didn't you?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.410
Mom said it was great.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.390
Oh, good to hear!

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.860
Do your mom and the twins 
ever come to your games?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.320
Not sure they ever will.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.680
Things are really busy back home.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.690
So,

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.610
we third-years will be 
retiring as of today!

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.950
The first-years will have their 
debut competition in late September,

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.310
so don't let your guard down!

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.120
Okay!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:38.190
We'd like Yoda to be the 
next club president.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:38.970
Yes!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.020
As for vice president...

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.760
<i>Yoda-san is the only second-year, so...</i>

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.910
<i>...the vice president will 
be one of us first-years.</i>

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.240
<i>It'll be Mikage.</i>

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.820
<i>She's the group's best rider, after all.</i>

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.450
<i>I guess the odds are one in five.</i>

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.840
<i>I hope I don't get chosen...</i>

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.890
Hachiken, we're counting on you.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.320
Huh, wait!

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.190
What?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.820
Congrats!

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.570
Good luck, Hachiken.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:04.820
Yo, Vice Prez!

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.080
Good luck!

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.980
Ooezo Agricultural High School 
 <b>Equestrian Club 
 </b>Club Journal

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.990
Why me?

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.400
Mikage's so much better at riding.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.100
This isn't about who's good.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.460
Vice presidents build consensus.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.770
Hachiken, for better or worse, 
you're an honest guy, right?

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:23.470
Huh?

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.620
I'm... rather cynical.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.300
Even about things like
 picking this school.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.770
Even your cynicism is honest.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:30.670
Put another way,

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.250
you're kind of obvious.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:38.010
Well, that's why it's easy to trust you.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.840
Everyone will find you easy to 
talk to if they have any problems.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.400
Of course we thought about 
Mikage as vice president, too.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.620
But, how should I put it...

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.080
Even though she's easygoing,

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.360
she kind of doesn't let 
people get too close, right?

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.170
I-Is that right?

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.370
Really?

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:57.620
Call it a woman's intuition.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.280
I'm skeptical.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.930
Have more confidence, Hachiken!

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.380
Because of the whole 
pizza and bacon thing,

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.770
some of taken to calling you
 "the guy who never says no"!

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:08.670
Me?!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.550
Oh, that sounds kind of cool!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.880
So he never turns anyone away?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.150
It just goes to show how much 
people trust you, okay?

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.020
Please become the vice president.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.520
Good luck, Man Who Can't Say No!

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.400
Huh?

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.150
Just one word change, 
and I'm now an indecisive guy?

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.170
<i>I wonder if I'm cut out to 
be the vice president...</i>

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.030
It just goes to show how much 
people trust you, okay?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.660
Please become the vice president.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:45.170
Wh...

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.250
Incoming Message 
1/1

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.750
Message Received 
 1/1

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.010
Message0001
Date/Time: 9/3 18:15
Frm: Mom 
 Sub: The bacon arrived 

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.650
<b>It was delicious. 
 I had Dad try some. 
 He said it was good.</b>

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.170
Wh-Wh-Wh-What's the matter, Mikage?!

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.500
Oh, um, it's nothing.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.430
Nothing?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.180
Komaba, did you do something to her?!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.910
I didn't do anything.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.850
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.110
H-Hey!

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:45.330
Oh...

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.850
Um, are you okay?

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.220
I'm fine.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.370
Don't worry about me!

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.740
Honestly, it's nothing.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.000
What the hell?

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.470
Honestly, it's nothing.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.470
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:30.230
<i>Man, I didn't sleep enough because 
I had too much on my mind.</i>

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:34.150
Morning.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.280
Oh, morning.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:43.890
Um—

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.770
I'm glad it cleared up!

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.440
Yeah.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:50.650
About yesterday—

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.260
Oh, and you're now the vice president!

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.500
Y-You're right!

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:57.960
I can't believe it. 
I wasn't in any clubs in junior high.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.510
I wonder if I'll do an okay 
job as vice president.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.040
You'll be fine.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.850
When you put your mind to it, 
you're really focused, Hachiken-kun!

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:07.280
Everyone trusts you, too.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.270
Um, if something's bothering you—

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.480
Morning!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.390
Huh, what's wrong, Hachiken?

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:16.420
Something bothering you?

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.960
<i>In the end, I couldn't ask her...</i>

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:27.980
And the two of them live right next
 to each other and are childhood friends.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:28.830
Yeah?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.110
He's the top ace of the baseball club,

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:33.660
and just as he'd promised the girl, 
he takes her to the national tournament.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.800
It's cool when the protagonist isn't all talk!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.540
So what happens to them in the end?

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.590
They get together.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.590
Well, yeah.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.500
It's nice when they're living 
next to each other and

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:46.850
their parents are fine with it all.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.320
It's heartwarming.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:51.370
The nearest house to mine 
is three kilometers away.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.270
Having anyone come all the way over

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.150
to wake me up is like a dream come true.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:59.080
I'll go pay my respects to 
your family at some point.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.280
Okay, got it.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.410
I'm sorry to put you through this.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:06.390
I'm fine.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.980
Don't worry, Icchan!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.910
Actually, Hachiken-kun is worried.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.270
Hachiken, worried?

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.260
Did you tell him about us?

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.920
No, it doesn't involve him, anyway...

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:18.990
But...

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.530
Well, I was crying.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:25.260
Why's he such a busybody?

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.610
It's not like he can do 
anything if he finds out.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.850
<b>Men's Restroom</b>

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:48.570
What?!

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.800
I'm waiting my turn.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.500
Don't be so passive-aggressive!

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.560
You wanna say something?

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:55.540
About yesterday...

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.990
Like I said, it was nothing.

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.300
How can it be about nothing?!

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.800
You and Mikage looked so serious!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.720
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.890
Semester Finals 
Math

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.470
Okay, time's up!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.800
Pass your exams forward.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.470
Finals done!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.950
Aki, math was so hard.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.150
Yeah.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.510
Tokiwa, did you make it?

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.320
I'm different this time around!

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:30.620
Wow, Hachiken-kun's 
tutoring must've paid off!

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.120
Tokiwa...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.220
I used a secret weapon this time!

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.710
Congrats on finishing finals!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.800
Yeah!

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:48.270
Why does this school hold a barbecue 
every time there are exams?

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.740
Maybe it's the carrot after the stick.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.020
That's how they brainwash you.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.190
Komaba, how'd your exams go?

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.540
I'll definitely pass!

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.290
After finally making 
it into the lineup,

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.570
it'd be stupid if Ds got me banned 
from club activities!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.530
Right!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.310
Good luck at your match!

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.990
<i>Komaba is his usual self.</i>

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.240
<i>But Mikage was crying...</i>

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.660
Where were we supposed to 
take these boxes again?

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.720
Komaba might be pitching 
in the next game.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.630
I think they said to the back.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.630
Really?

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.480
He's kind of cool.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.560
What, do you want to hook up with him?

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.430
Mikage-chan, didn't you go 
to the same junior high?

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:29.520
Does Komaba have a girlfriend?

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.060
I don't think he's dating 
anyone right now.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.190
Maybe I'll go talk to him, then.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:36.970
Really?

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.270
I'll be cheering for you!

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.770
<i>Is there nothing going on?!</i>

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.070
<i>Or is there some secret 
that only they know?</i>

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.240
<i>What's going on between them, anyway?</i>

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:48.490
<i>Is this jealousy?!</i>

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.340
<i>No, I'm not being that selfish.</i>

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.630
<i>I'm just worried about 
Mikage, that's all.</i>

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:53.670
<i>No, wait...</i>

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.000
<i>If I'm worried about her,</i>

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.250
<i>it must mean I like her and 
have ulterior motives...</i>

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.210
Hachiken, you're late!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.670
What's wrong?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.790
What's it mean to like someone?

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:06.810
You're thinking about something 
complicated again, aren't you?

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:06.690
Liking someone...

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:08.720
Is it "like" or "love"?

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:10.990
I like chickens!

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:12.000
Cows for me.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:12.810
Cows.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:13.780
Pigs.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:15.600
You don't have to throw away 
any parts, so I like that.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.680
You guys like whatever's profitable, don't you?!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.690
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.610
The baseball club has returned!

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.150
Ah, good job.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.630
Komaba, your mother called.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.620
She asked you to call back.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.610
Okay, thank you.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.620
Oh, Komaba.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:37.910
What is it?

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.540
Can I talk with you for a sec?

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.240
Man, she's definitely 
got the hots for Komaba.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.910
He's popular with the ladies.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.580
He might become the next 
ace player, after all.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.880
Sure, and I don't even get 
picked to be a benchwarmer.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.090
Man...

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.520
I want a girlfriend.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.740
Hey, it's time for the next group!

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.610
Get out already!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.840
No!

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:07.520
Hey.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.490
You're gonna pitch on Sunday, right?

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:10.780
Good luck!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.590
Thanks.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:12.630
And?

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.110
Huh?

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.120
How'd things turn out earlier 
with Nakaya from Agriculture?

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:18.330
Didn't she ask you out?

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:21.120
Oh, I turned her down.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:24.140
Man, the future ace 
player is in no rush!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.590
So that means...

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.770
God dammit!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.500
you have someone else you like... or...

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:30.130
I'd be... I'd be, too.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.130
I don't!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.090
I've got my hands full 
with the upcoming match!

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.760
I don't have time for a girlfriend!

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.220
All right, let's go!

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:42.020
Yeah!

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:43.260
Komaba.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.140
Yes, sir!

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.610
If you can get five scoreless innings,

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.010
dinner's on me!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:48.980
Okay!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.360
Meat again?

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.840
The all-you-can-eat kind.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:52.740
The usual...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.320
It'll be sushi this time!

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:56.220
Leave it to us, Komaba!

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:57.910
You can let 'em hit!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.790
We'll be sure to run around 
to work up a huge appetite!

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.710
Let's have a good game!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.970
Ezonoo's pitcher is a first-year.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:07.420
He's freakin' tall.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.710
I heard he pitched a good 
game at the first match.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.410
Being able to save their ace, even at 
the third game, is a nice advantage.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:17.850
I played against 
Komaba in junior high,

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:18.930
but he wasn't that—

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.220
Strike!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:31.480
Sushi, sushi, sushi...

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.670
What the...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:31.060
Freaky.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.220
Another miss!

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.550
It's the fourth strike-out 
for Komaba-kun today!

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.240
Whoa!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.620
Yeah!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.430
After five innings, it's 3 to 0,

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.060
with Ezonoo in the lead.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.410
Komaba-kun, a first-year, 
is continuing his good pitching!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.200
Man, he's amazing.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.980
He's been staying behind late 
to do extra practice lately.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.070
He's really into it.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.940
What's wrong with being greedy?!

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:57.170
I'm going to reinvigorate... 
our business!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.180
Yo!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.970
Oh, Ookawa-senpai.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.210
What's up?

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:06.640
Oh, just curious how my 
darling juniors were doing.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.910
Good job, everyone! Oh, hey, Ookawa.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.090
Senpai, what about your job search?

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.640
Guys, quit slacking and 
listening to the radio!

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.240
Oh, no! The ball got past him!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.100
Ezonoo has no outs, with players 
on first and third base.

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.590
This is their chance to widen the lead!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.450
Just this once, okay?

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.080
Yeah!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:24.410
We won!

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:28.770
All right, it's our turn to 
work hard and practice...

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:34.800
They got out!

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:35.840
What?!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.160
Oh...

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.530
Shoot...

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:40.140
I forgot to close the gate...

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.210
Crap!

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.930
They'll get into the soilage!

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.100
C'mon! Catch them, quick!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.270
Thank goodness nothing 
really bad happened...

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.660
but if they'd gotten 
out onto the roads,

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.490
it could've been a disaster!

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:56.740
Right, I'm sorry.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:03.740
It's unusual to see Aki 
make a mistake like that.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:10.050
Some students struggle to 
talk about how they feel,

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:11.950
even though they're suffering.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.000
If you notice anyone like that,
 please help them.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.690
Everyone will find you easy to talk 
to if they have any problems.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:17.970
Have more confidence, Hachiken!

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.390
<i>I'm the vice president...</i>

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.500
<i>I'm supposed to be the 
consensus builder,</i>

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:27.070
<i>and if anyone's troubled by anything, 
I want to be able to listen.</i>

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:29.570
<i>I've gotta be brave!</i>

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:30.810
<i>Okay!</i>

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.400
Mikage!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.900
What were you talking about 
with Komaba the other day?

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:39.480
Oh, right.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:41.200
Nothing that involves you, Hachiken-kun.

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.650
Good job, everyone!

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:47.410
Thanks!

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.060
How'd your exams turn out?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.280
<i>Did I just work myself up for nothing?</i>

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.500
Did he lose a horseshoe?

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.000
Oh!

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.870
I wonder if the nails came loose.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.490
We'll have to get him reshod tomorrow.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.440
Y-Yeah.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.970
Congrats, Hachiken-kun.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:20.740
They say it's good luck when 
you find a lost horseshoe.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.130
Really?

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:25.650
It can ward off evil, 
make you lucky with money,

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:28.290
and even protect you 
from traffic accidents.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:29.240
How's that?

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.680
They say that's because 
horses don't step on people.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.120
Huh...

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:37.450
That's not all.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.580
There are horses who limp 
over to their riders

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:43.300
after a fall on a broken leg 
because they were worried.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.670
But a horse with a broken leg 
gets put down, right?

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.250
Yeah...

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.250
But even then, they'll do things like that.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.980
Horses care about their friends.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:00.080
You should put that on your door
 with the branches up.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.260
It'll bring you luck!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.700
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:08.430
A lucky charm, huh?

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.030
<i>I was trying to cheer her up,</i>

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.760
<i>but I just got cheered up in return.</i>

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:16.580
Okay,

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.480
I'll have to give this a try!

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:50.330
This story is a work of fiction.
